  <h2>What a modpack launcher does</h2>
  <p>A modpack is more than just a list of mods. It includes specific versions of each mod, configs that make them play nicely, custom recipes, scripted progression, sometimes resource packs and shaders. Installing one by hand means downloading every file, setting up the mod loader, allocating Java memory, and praying nothing conflicts. A modpack launcher does it all in one click.</p>

  <h2>How GDLauncher installs modpacks</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open GDLauncher, click <strong>+ New Instance</strong></li>
    <li>Open the modpack browser. Search for the pack you want. RLCraft, All The Mods 10, Better MC, FTB Skies, anything on CurseForge or Modrinth.</li>
    <li>Click Install. GDLauncher downloads every mod, the matching Minecraft version, the correct mod loader, the right Java runtime, and applies the configs.</li>
    <li>Wait a minute or two for downloads. Hit Play.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>If the pack needs more RAM than the default, bump it in instance settings → Java. <a href="/guides/allocate-more-ram">See the RAM guide</a>.</p>

  <h2>Popular modpacks GDLauncher supports out of the box</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>All The Mods 10 (ATM10)</strong>: kitchen sink with hundreds of mods, NeoForge, 8-12 GB RAM</li>
